{# Regular events — classes, clubs, weekly markets — grouped by day.

   Renders nothing when there are none, so it is safe to leave in place.

   These are fixtures, not events: they never appear in the upcoming list,
   because a weekly class expanded into dated occurrences would bury the
   one-off events the page exists to show. Grouping by day is also how
   people actually think about them ("what's on a Tuesday?").

   Only currently-active regulars appear — see the from/until/except
   fields in events.json. A class that stopped for the summer stops
   showing on its own. #}

{# The section renders even when the list is empty, because the invitation
   below is the point of it. It previously carried a made-up yoga class as
   sample data, which was removed on 29 Aug 2026: an invented event is worse
   than an invented listing, because somebody turns up. Nothing goes in here
   that has not been told to us by whoever runs it. #}
{% set byDay = events.regulars | regularsByDay %}
<section class="wrap" id="regulars" aria-labelledby="regulars-h">
  <h2 id="regulars-h">Regular classes and groups</h2>
  <div class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  {% if byDay | length %}
  <p class="page-intro">Classes, clubs and groups that meet regularly. Anything
  open to the public in Largs can be listed here, free — see below to add one.</p>
  {% else %}
  <p class="page-intro">Nothing listed here yet. Classes, clubs and groups that
  meet regularly in Largs can go here, free — see below to add one.</p>
  {% endif %}

  {% for group in byDay %}
  <div class="regular-day">
    <h3 class="regular-dayname">{{ group.day }}</h3>
    {% for r in group.items %}
    <article class="regular">
      {% if r.time %}<div class="regular-time">{{ r.time }}</div>{% endif %}
      {# Same column order as a dated event — see .event-main in site.css. #}
      <div class="event-main">
        {% if r.image %}<img class="event-img" src="{{ r.image }}" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">{% endif %}
        <div class="regular-body">
          <h4 class="regular-title">{{ r.title }}</h4>
          {% if r.venue or r.freq %}<p class="regular-meta">{{ r.venue }}{% if r.venue and r.freq %} · {% endif %}{{ r.freq }}</p>{% endif %}
          {% if r.blurb %}<p class="regular-blurb">{{ r.blurb }}</p>{% endif %}
          {# `contact` is either plain text (a phone number, "ask at the
             counter") or {label, url} for a link — the same shape the
             directory uses. A string has no .url, so the test is safe for
             both. Without this a URL printed as a raw address. #}
          {% if r.contact %}<p class="regular-contact">
            {%- if r.contact.url %}<a href="{{ r.contact.url }}" rel="noopener">{{ r.contact.label }} →</a>
            {%- else %}{{ r.contact }}{% endif -%}
          </p>{% endif %}
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</section>
